            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.77,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In 1000 calendar years, how many years are divisible by 400? 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.846,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In 1000 calendar years, how many years are divisible by 100 but not divisible by 400? 10 – 2 = 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.151,
            0.846,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In 1000 calendar years, how many years are divisible by 4 but not divisible by 100 and 400? 250 – 10 = 240."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.189,
            0.638,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The rest of the years are 1000 – (2 + 8 + 240) = 750."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.213,
            0.698,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the total number of days in 1000 calendar years is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.232,
            0.796,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(750 × 365) + (240 × 366) + (8 × 365) + (2 × 366) = 3,65,242 days."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.257,
            0.847,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Earth needs 3,65,242.2 days to go around the Sun 1000 times. Hence, in 1000 years, the calendar year is slightly shorter (by 0.2 days) than the actual number of days the Earth takes to go around the Sun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.333,
            0.847,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The calendar makers did not want to bother about a small difference that would happen in 1000 years! So, they left the scheme of leap years as is …"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.409,
            0.545,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Making Yet Another Adjustment"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
